[Id "slav"]
[Name "Slav Defense"]
[Side "black"]
[ECO "D10-D19"]
[Description "Defend the d5 pawn with …c6, keeping the c8 bishop free to develop."]
[Tags "solid, positional"]

1. d4 d5 2. c4 c6 {…c6 supports d5 without blocking the c8 bishop, unlike …e6.} 3. Nf3
  (3. cxd5 {@variation Exchange} 3... cxd5 {…cxd5 keeps a symmetrical, very solid pawn structure.} 4. Nc3 Nf6 5. Bf4 Nc6 {…Nc6 develops and adds a defender to d4 and e5.} 6. e3 Bf5 {…Bf5 mirrors White's active bishop.} 7. Nf3 e6
{@line id=slav-exchange level=1 tier=main name="Exchange (3.cxd5)" summary="Symmetry is fine for Black: develop knights and bishop actively, then …e6."}
8. Qb3 Bb4 {…Bb4 counters the queen's attack on b7 by pinning the c3 knight.} 9. Bb5 O-O {…O-O: Black lets White take on c6 and recaptures with the b-pawn.}
{@line id=slav-exchange-deep level=2 tier=main name="8.Qb3" summary="Against Qb3 and Bb5, pin with …Bb4 and castle; the position stays balanced."}
)
3... Nf6 4. Nc3
  (4. e3 {@variation Quiet 4.e3} 4... Bf5 {…Bf5: White's e3 shut in their own bishop, so Black gets this bishop out at once.} 5. Nc3 e6 6. Nh4 Bg6 {…Bg6 keeps the bishop; Black is happy to recapture towards the centre.} 7. Nxg6 hxg6 {…hxg6 opens the h-file for Black's rook and gives a solid pawn structure.}
{@line id=slav-4e3 level=1 tier=main name="Quiet 4.e3" summary="Against 4.e3, play …Bf5 at once; if White's knight chases it, recapture with …hxg6."}
)
4... dxc4 {…dxc4 takes the pawn when White can't easily win it back with tempo.} {@variation Main Line} 5. a4
  (5. e3 b5 {…b5 holds the extra c4 pawn for now.} 6. a4 b4 {…b4 kicks the knight to a poor square on the rim.} 7. Na2 e6 8. Bxc4 Be7 {…Be7 develops; Black plans …O-O and …c5.}
{@line id=slav-5e3 level=2 tier=side name="5.e3 b5" summary="When White plays slowly with 5.e3, hold the pawn with …b5, then kick the knight with …b4."}
)
5... Bf5 {…Bf5 develops the bishop before …e6.} 6. e3
  (6. Ne5 Nbd7 {…Nbd7 challenges the e5 knight right away.} 7. Nxc4 Qc7 {…Qc7 supports the …e5 push.} 8. g3 e5 {…e5 frees Black's game in the centre.}
{@line id=slav-krause level=2 tier=side name="Krause (6.Ne5)" summary="Against 6.Ne5, challenge the knight with …Nbd7, then free your game with …Qc7 and …e5."}
)
6... e6 7. Bxc4 Bb4 {…Bb4 pins the c3 knight and stops White's e4 push.}
{@line id=slav-main level=1 tier=main name="Main Line (5.a4 Bf5)" summary="Take on c4, develop the bishop to f5 before …e6, then pin with …Bb4."}
8. O-O O-O 9. Qe2 Nbd7 {…Nbd7 prepares for e4 by covering e5.} 10. e4 Bg6 {…Bg6 steps back from the pawn's attack, still eyeing e4.} 11. Bd3 Bh5 {…Bh5 pins the f3 knight, so White's e5 push leaves d4 weaker.}
{@line id=slav-main-deep level=2 tier=main name="9.Qe2" summary="When White pushes e4, retreat the bishop to g6 and then pin with …Bh5."} *
